From 4aef229844068e69fd6c66a1b7533cdfcbf19f0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:30:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Family repairs and the structural validator (U12)

Devotion ids repaired, then frozen:
- family-devotions-2.json: the second "forgiveness" and "obedience" become
  "when-someone-hurts-you" and "trusting-enough-to-obey" (the twelve on
  /family keep theirs), and the Genesis 1 devotion is retitled "God Called
  It Good" so two devotions no longer share "Made On Purpose".
- scripts/data/family-devotion-ids.json records all 72 ids. The family gate
  fails when one is removed or renamed without a vercel.json redirect from
  /family/devotions/<id> to the devotion that replaces it, because a printed
  card's QR code cannot be recalled. `--freeze` adds new ids, never removes.

validate-family.mjs globs client/public/family-*.json instead of listing
files, and checks unique devotion ids and titles, unique catechism questions
(the five known repeats flagged for U40), age bands where claimed, counts
that match copy (plan lengths; every "N questions" said of the catechism and
"N weekly devotions" anywhere in pages, components, the catalogue, the
printables and llms.txt), one translation per surface (each family page's
ScriptureNote names exactly its libraries' translation), no em-dash or "--"
outside quoted Scripture, and the year map once U10 generates it. The BSB
checks are unchanged.

Pages:
- The catechism's "this week" walks all 76 questions and starts again
  (lib/familyCatechism.ts), so Q53 to Q76 get their weeks; 2026 keeps the
  question it already showed.
- /family/devotions, /family/catechism and /family/reading-plans load through
  fetchJson with LoadFailed and a retry instead of an endless "Loading...".
- /family/devotions numbers each devotion "1 of 72" instead of "Week 72";
  the hero says seventy-two, more than a year of them.
- The four family heroes use --charcoal-fg and --charcoal-fg-muted instead
  of rgba() and --bone.
- Catalogue: "A 76-question family catechism" (it said 52).
- Parenting Stage Guide: "Ages 1 to 3" and so on (it said "Ages 1--3").

Tests: server/family-gate.test.ts (the gate passes as committed and fails on
each seeded fault, a duplicate id first), lib/familyCatechism.test.ts, and
pages/family-pages.test.tsx (failed load, retry, numbering, a question past
52 in its week).

